xnu 0342: blank the panel with DCS instead of painting the framebuffer black

Measured 2026-11-16 on the phone with mondrianfb_blank=30: 30 s after the last
present the panel reads black, a touch is delivered (the ring logs
`MONDRIAN HID: touch 0 down`), and the framebuffer never changes again -- no
`MONDRIAN FB: panel wake` line at all, because the wake lives inside present()
and iOS, which has already dimmed and stopped its own display link, presents
nothing after the touch. The black paint is what makes that final: it destroys
the only frame the panel could show.

The panel is a DCS command panel, so switch it off with 0x28 and back on with
0x29. Off, it keeps its own RAM; on, it shows the last frame again without
waiting for a present. Input un-blanks the driver state at once and the tick
sends 0x29 on the thread that already sends the brightness DCS. A panel that
refuses 0x28 keeps the old black-paint fallback, so the change cannot make the
blank worse than it was.

The DMA helper grows the MIPI short form (data type 0x05, the command in the
first packet byte, four bytes on the wire); display on and off take no
parameter and a long write with two NOP bytes is not what the standard says.
